{title: Jesus, Victor at the Cross}
{author: Chi-Ming Chien}

{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
Dm C Bb F/A G

{comment: Verse 1}
                                
May the [C]broken [G/B]ones among us meet the Hea[Am]ler,
And the [Dm]thirsty drink the [F]water of new [G]Life.
Grant [C]those who grieve to [G/B]meet the risen [Am]Savior.
Let [Dm]all who chance upon [F] us meet the [G]Christ.

{comment: Chorus}
[C]Je[G]sus, [Am]victor at the [F] cross
Holy Red[C/E]eem[G]er, we [F]count all else as [G]loss.
We have [E/G#]tasted living [Am]bread,
At your [G/B]banquet all are [F/C]fed[C]--
[Bb]May your king[F/Bb]dom come[C].

{comment: Verse 2}
Let the [C]way of weakness [G/B]be for us a [Am]treasure,
Since the [Dm]life laid down is [F]raised again a[G]new.
Pour [C]out your Holy [G/B]Spirit without [Am]measure,
As [Dm]we live out the [F]life that comes from [G]you.

{comment: Chorus}
[C]Je[G]sus, [Am]victor at the [F] cross
Holy Red[C/E]eem[G]er, we [F]count all else as [G]loss.
So that [E/G#]we may know you, [Am]Christ--
Bear your [G/B]cross and share your [F/C]li[C]fe.
[Bb]May your will[F/Bb] be done[C].

{comment: Verse 3}
Let the [C]stranger find his [G/B]welcome as a [Am]brother;
And the [Dm]outcast, in the [F]church, a sister [G]be.
Let the [C]powers that see the Chu[G/B]rch's witness [Am]tremble
As [Dm]we display God's [F]new humani[G]ty.

{comment: Chorus}
[C]Je[G]sus, [Am]victor at the [F] cross
Holy Red[C/E]eem[G]er, your [F]life for us has [G]brought
All div[E/G#]isions to an [Am]end,
Proclaimed the [G/B]peace that you int[F/C]end[C].
[Bb]May your king[F/Bb]dom [C]come,
[Bb]May your will[F/Bb] be [C]done,
[Bb]May your king[F/Bb]dom [C]come,

